Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 14:06:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Daily posting: never auto-release ambiguous claims;
 moderator two-click recovery
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Revised per review of fad13b2 (new commit, no amend):

- Claim state machine: pre-submit -> submitting -> done. 'submitting' is set
  immediately BEFORE the Reddit call; from there the outcome is unknowable to
  later runs, so it is NEVER released automatically and NEVER auto-recreated,
  at any age. The only auto-released state is a stale (>15 min) pre-submit
  claim — the holder died before any Reddit call (confirmed pre-submission
  failure). A throw from submitCustomPost is no longer treated as a confirmed
  pre-submission failure: the claim is retained as uncertain.
- Reconciliation identity verified, no username convention: the SDK exposes
  no app-account username API (grep-verified), so crash-window recovery
  enumerates the installation's OWN subreddit via reddit.getNewPosts
  ({subredditName: context.subredditName}) and adopts a post matching BOTH
  the UTC day and the challenge id (ids recur every 34 days — postData now
  carries {challengeId, day, v}, all public and answer-independent).
  Absence in a listing is not proof of non-existence -> still uncertain.
- Uncertain days: retained claim (TTL refreshed), loud '[rangefinder:
  dailypost] UNCERTAIN DAY' scheduler log, explicit status to all callers.
  Moderator recovery via the EXISTING menu item: first click arms a 2-minute
  override and shows instructions; second click performs one final
  reconciliation and only then (human-confirmed) clears the claim and creates
  a replacement. No duplicate menu item; no automatic duplicate creation.
- Legacy claims from the previous revision honoured conservatively (with
  postId -> done; without -> submitting/un certain path).
- Tests: 22 daily-post cases covering crash-after-accept (adoption success
  and failure), creator overrun >15 min, concurrent scheduled+moderator,
  repeated delivery, pre-submit release, override adoption + override
  replacement, legacy/corrupt claims, unreachable reconciliation, day+challenge
  match discipline (unit total 70/70).
- Runbook D3 and README document the at-most-once vs availability trade-off
  and the worst-case bound (player results/stats keyed by challenge, not post).

Battery: lint 0, tsc 0, build OK, spec 18/18, unit 70/70, harness 8/8,
audit:bundle OK. Local only — NOT pushed.

